                                        "entry_id": "006dbfd6-0e9c-32d3-b64a-aa622f19ba7b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Turdus torquatus, a European thrush, similar to the common blackbird, but with a ring of white feathers at its neck."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f314251a-fd58-44a5-80bd-ca4ce2371004",
                                                "sense_id": "e5b55f71-dc3c-328b-b3ec-fc9b89fb99ed",
                                                "text": "Some birds seem to belong to all scenery alike; others love only the waste common land, the stream, or the sea-shore; while a third division, οἱ εκλετόι (the elect), are only to be found in one or two favoured counties in the whole of England. Of these last are the Ring-Ouzels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c9576c3-3ee8-4f21-b27a-e25df084a79f",
                                                "sense_id": "e5b55f71-dc3c-328b-b3ec-fc9b89fb99ed",
                                                "text": "In recording my observations on the Ring-Ouzel (Turdus torquatus), I have no expectation of writing anything original. But I think it possible that personal notes on this interesting bird may be acceptable to those ornithologists who are less familiar with it than I am."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
